---
description: Depot NixOS Service Template
globs: *.nix
---
# Depot NixOS Service Template

Rules for creating new NixOS services following the depot standard structure.

<rule>
name: nixos_service_template
description: Standards for creating new NixOS services
filters:
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "infra/nixos-modules/.*\\.nix$"
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "services/.*/machine/.*\\.nix$"
  - type: file_path
    pattern: "services/.*/machine/README\\.md$"
actions:
  - type: reject
    conditions:
      - pattern: "^[^#]"
        message: "License header missing at file start"
      - pattern: "mkOption(?!.*type)"
        message: "mkOption must specify a type"
      - pattern: "serviceConfig(?!.*Restart)"
        message: "serviceConfig should specify Restart behavior"
      - pattern: "wantedBy(?!.*multi-user\\.target)"
        message: "Service should be wanted by multi-user.target by default"

  - type: suggest
    message: |
      Follow these conventions when creating a new NixOS service:

      1. File Structure:
         Create these files under infra/nixos-modules/ or services/YOUR_SERVICE/machine/:
         - service-name.nix (main module)
         - vm.nix (VM/ISO configuration)
         - test.nix (test suite)
         - README.md (documentation)

      2. Module Structure:
         ```nix
         # Copyright (c) YEAR Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
         # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary

         # NixOS module for SERVICE_DESCRIPTION
         { depot, pkgs, config, lib, ... }:

         let
           inherit (builtins) attrValues mapAttrs;
           inherit (lib)
             concatStringsSep
             mkEnableOption
             mkIf
             mkOption
             types;

           cfg = config.services.depot.SERVICE_NAME;
           description = "SERVICE_DESCRIPTION";

           # Helper functions for argument preparation
           prepareArgs = args:
             concatStringsSep " "
               (attrValues (mapAttrs (key: value: "-${key} \"${toString value}\"")
                 args));
         in
         {
           options.services.depot.SERVICE_NAME = {
             enable = mkEnableOption description;

             # Required configuration options
             args = mkOption {
               type = types.attrsOf types.str;
               description = "Key value pairs for command line arguments";
             };

             # Optional configuration with defaults
             secretsFile = mkOption {
               type = types.str;
               default = config.age.secretsDir + "/SERVICE_NAME";
               description = "Path to secrets file";
             };
         };

           config = mkIf cfg.enable {
             systemd.services.SERVICE_NAME = {
               inherit description;

               # Service configuration
               script = "${pkgs.SERVICE_NAME}/bin/SERVICE_NAME ${prepareArgs cfg.args}";
               wantedBy = [ "multi-user.target" ];

               serviceConfig = {
                 # Standard service configuration
                 Restart = "always";
                 StateDirectory = "SERVICE_NAME";
                 DynamicUser = true;

                 # Security settings
                 LoadCredential = "secrets:${cfg.secretsFile}";

                 # Hardening options
                 CapabilityBoundingSet = "";
                 LockPersonality = true;
                 NoNewPrivileges = true;
                 PrivateDevices = true;
                 PrivateTmp = true;
                 ProtectClock = true;
                 ProtectControlGroups = true;
                 ProtectHome = true;
                 ProtectHostname = true;
                 ProtectKernelLogs = true;
                 ProtectKernelModules = true;
                 ProtectKernelTunables = true;
                 ProtectSystem = "strict";
                 RestrictAddressFamilies = [ "AF_INET" "AF_INET6" ];
                 RestrictNamespaces = true;
                 RestrictRealtime = true;
                 RestrictSUIDSGID = true;
                 SystemCallArchitectures = "native";
                 SystemCallFilter = [ "@system-service" ];
                 UMask = "0077";
               };
             };
           };
         }
         ```

      3. Service Configuration Best Practices:
         - Use mkEnableOption for the enable flag
         - Define clear types for all options
         - Use descriptive option names
         - Provide meaningful defaults where appropriate
         - Document all options
         - Use systemd hardening options
         - Handle secrets securely
         - Implement proper argument handling

      4. Testing:
         ```nix
         # test.nix
         let
           nixpkgs = import <nixpkgs> {
             config.allowUnfree = true;
           };
         in
         import (nixpkgs.path + "/nixos/tests/make-test-python.nix") (
           { pkgs, ... }: {
             name = "SERVICE_NAME";

             nodes.machine = { config, pkgs, ... }: {
               imports = [ ./service-name.nix ];

               services.depot.SERVICE_NAME = {
                 enable = true;
                 args = {
                   # Test configuration
                 };
               };
             };

             testScript = ''
               start_all()

               # Wait for service to start
               machine.wait_for_unit("SERVICE_NAME.service")

               # Basic service tests
               machine.succeed("systemctl is-active SERVICE_NAME.service")

               # Custom test cases
               ...
             '';
           }
         )
         ```

      5. Documentation:
         ```markdown
         # SERVICE_NAME

         NixOS module for SERVICE_DESCRIPTION.

         ## Usage

         Enable the service in your NixOS configuration:

         ```nix
         services.depot.SERVICE_NAME = {
           enable = true;
           args = {
             # Required configuration
           };
         };
         ```

         ## Options

         | Option | Type | Default | Description |
         |--------|------|---------|-------------|
         | enable | boolean | false | Enable the service |
         | args | attrs | - | Service arguments |
         | secretsFile | string | "/run/agenix/SERVICE_NAME" | Path to secrets |

         ## Security

         This service:
         - Runs as a dynamic user
         - Uses systemd credentials for secrets
         - Implements standard systemd hardening options
         ```

examples:
  - input: |
      # Bad: Missing license header and description
      { pkgs, ... }:
      {
        options.services.myservice.enable = true;
      }

      # Good: Complete module with proper structure
      # Copyright (c) 2024 Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary

      # NixOS module for My Service Description
      { depot, pkgs, config, lib, ... }:

      let
        cfg = config.services.depot.myservice;
        description = "My Service Description";
      in
      {
        options.services.depot.myservice = {
          enable = mkEnableOption description;
        };

        config = mkIf cfg.enable {
          systemd.services.myservice = {
            inherit description;
            wantedBy = [ "multi-user.target" ];
            serviceConfig.Restart = "always";
          };
        };
      }

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 2.0
</rule>

